R1. How many molecules must decide together? (Delta >= 2, physics wins 97.7%)
  PVED taken as 2.3e-14 J/mol (g = 1e-17 at 0 C); modern range spans ~1e-19..1e-16 in g
  T=273 K: g=1.0e-17, need N >= 3.6e+33 molecules (5.9e+09 mol); at 1e-06 M a well-mixed 6e+12 m^3 (cube 18 km), at 0.001 M a well-mixed 6e+09 m^3 (cube 1.8 km), at 0.1 M a well-mixed 6e+07 m^3 (cube 0.39 km)
  T=300 K: g=9.1e-18, need N >= 4.3e+33 molecules (7.2e+09 mol); at 1e-06 M a well-mixed 7e+12 m^3 (cube 19 km), at 0.001 M a well-mixed 7e+09 m^3 (cube 1.9 km), at 0.1 M a well-mixed 7e+07 m^3 (cube 0.42 km)
  T=373 K: g=7.3e-18, need N >= 6.7e+33 molecules (1.1e+10 mol); at 1e-06 M a well-mixed 1e+13 m^3 (cube 22 km), at 0.001 M a well-mixed 1e+10 m^3 (cube 2.2 km), at 0.1 M a well-mixed 1e+08 m^3 (cube 0.48 km)
  -> a warm little pond (1 m^3 at 1 M holds 6e26) is ~7 orders short; only ocean-scale water that
     is mixed on the decision time can pool enough molecules. Time helps only as (k tau)^1/4.

R2. Bennu/Ryugu are racemic. Would the same amplifier have finished there?
  Bennu parent body c*tau = 3e+08 .. 9e+11 M s -> any amplifier with k2 >= 1e-11 .. 3e-08 /M/s would have finished there
  patches after alteration (pore diffusion only): 977-3090 m across -> a gram sample would sit
  inside one patch and show a large excess of either hand. Bennu's chiral amino acids (incl. isovaline,
  which cannot racemize afterwards) are racemic -> no such amplifier finished there.
  rate k2 drawn over 1e-06..1 /M/s:
    Enceladus          wins  22% | Bennu stays racemic   0% | both  0.0% | P(win | Bennu racemic)   0% | c*tau above Bennu's max in 1%
    Europa             wins  28% | Bennu stays racemic   0% | both  0.0% | P(win | Bennu racemic)   0% | c*tau above Bennu's max in 5%
    Early Earth ocean  wins  75% | Bennu stays racemic   0% | both  0.0% | P(win | Bennu racemic)   0% | c*tau above Bennu's max in 4%
  rate k2 drawn over 1e-12..1 /M/s:
    Enceladus          wins  14% | Bennu stays racemic  23% | both  0.4% | P(win | Bennu racemic)   2% | c*tau above Bennu's max in 1%
    Europa             wins  19% | Bennu stays racemic  23% | both  0.9% | P(win | Bennu racemic)   4% | c*tau above Bennu's max in 5%
    Early Earth ocean  wins  57% | Bennu stays racemic  23% | both  3.4% | P(win | Bennu racemic)  15% | c*tau above Bennu's max in 4%

