R6. Closed rock vs open ocean: does an amplified excess last? (frank2 network, A<->L/D reversible)
  closed, s = 1: K = 2                      : peak |ee| 0.70, above 10% of peak from ~8e+00 to ~7e+03 (model time ~ k2 c tau, see quench.py Q5); final +0.000
  closed, s = 0.01: K = 200 (slow reverse)  : peak |ee| 1.00, above 10% of peak from ~6e-01 to ~2e+06 (model time ~ k2 c tau, see quench.py Q5); final +0.000
  open (fed + outflow)                           : final ee +0.998  (held as long as the drive lasts)
  -> Bennu's parent body (closed, heat gone after ~10 Myr) stays racemic if its excess never rose
     (k2 c tau < rise time) OR rose and then faded (k2 c tau > fade time). Redo R2 with that rule:
